+
+### 16.14 Required Public Contract Group Publication
+
+The eight group identities and package addresses in REQ-P-PUBLIC-CONTRACTS-005
+are immutable Product publication projections of existing GTL, Validator,
+HoG, ABG, Product, transport and Public contract owners. The root and existing
+generic addresses remain available. A group entrypoint re-exports canonical
+owner definitions; it does not redeclare schema, validation, Runtime or Public
+function meaning. Source-to-group publication is typed against those owners.
+
+Product's existing public-contract publication module owns one static mapping
+from required identity/address to its canonical owner symbols and required
+content. The manifest generator consumes the emitted exact export closure,
+checks every required symbol/content and canonical asset relation, then adds
+the digest-bound native group row to the existing flat catalog. Its digest
+hashes the complete canonical (export, declaration path, declaration digest)
+inventory. An anchor symbol or address alias alone does not close a group.
+
+Every required serialized contract/vocabulary/corpus retains its own exact
+catalog identity and canonical owner-derived asset/definition locator.
+Native declarations and canonical schemas must agree. Missing content or an
+unproved later-symbol equivalence stops publication completeness; named later
+contracts require the versioned catalog and explicit supersession demanded by
+REQ-P-PUBLIC-CONTRACTS-004/-007A. No broad group replaces a schema locator.
+
+Capabilities remain projections of the existing Product-owned capability
+register/graph. Group membership adds only proved projection coordinates;
+PublicFunctionDefinition remains the sole closed public function authority.
+Binding an implemented subset does not discharge the existing mandatory-gap
+projection or establish complete 5.0 publication.
+
+The eight-row existing-owner/content/address map in the accepted publication
+design is this appendix's finite realization input. Complete unresolved
+native/schema/requirements-algebra owner relations before retaining their
+implementation. Reuse the existing catalog/native/asset/binding lifecycle;
+do not create a new package, runtime, registry, checker or qualification gate.
+
+Proof covers all required addresses and complete content, typed and canonical
+serialization/asset/native/catalog/capability correspondence, missing/crossed
+relations, and affected pack/install/ordinary carrier/cold read conservation.
+Root joins independently accepted parent and publication source scopes into
+one exact successor. Existing C09/Hello/Rust evidence stays at its own scope.
